.TH IOCTL_VALUE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
ioctl_value \- control a device with an integer argument
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/ioctl.h>
.B int ioctl_value(int descriptor, unsigned long request, unsigned long argument);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Like ioctl, but passes an integer rather than a pointer as the third
argument. The caller must use the argument type required by the request.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the request\-specific result, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ioctl (3crunch),
.BR ioctl (2)
